ges\\/1769430779845611520\\/lIgjSJGU_bigger.jpg"},"url":{"urlType":"DeepLink","url":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/xai"},"userLabelType":"BusinessLabel","userLabelDisplayType":"Badge"},"verified":false,"is_blue_verified":true,"verified_type":"Business"},"id":"3LhHjLAQQN6lGlWzfAsgMo8B2","conversation_preview":[{"message":"What is BRICS","sender":"USER","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]},{"message":"BRICS is an intergovernmental organization that originally comprised five countries: Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa. Over time, the group has expanded, with Egypt, Ethiopia, Iran, and the United Arab Emirates joining by January 2024, making the total membership nine countries, although Saudi Arabia delayed its membership decision as of that time. BRICS aims to be a counterpart and alternative to the G7 bloc, representing nearly half of the world\'s population and seeking to increase the influence of emerging economies in the global order. Here is a brief overview of BRICS based on the provided information:\\nFounding and Expansion: The term \'BRIC\' was initially used to highlight investment opportunities among Brazil, Russia, India, and China, with the first leaders\' summit held in Russia in 2009. South Africa joined in 2010, leading to the renaming to BRICS. By 2024, the bloc saw further expansion with new members joining.\\nEconomic Influence: BRICS represents a significant portion of the global economy, accounting for 46% of the world\'s population, 25% of the world\'s landmass, and had a substantial increase in economic growth from 1990 to 2019. In 2022, their share of the world GDP at purchasing power parity was 35.6%, and their intra-BRICS trade was valued at 614.8 billion USD.\\nObjectives and Initiatives: BRICS aims to coordinate economic and diplomatic policies, reduce dependency on the US dollar, and challenge its dominance in international trade by proposing initiatives like the BRICS Cross-Border Payment Initiative (BCBPI), which would use national currencies for trade among members. This is part of broader efforts to transform the international monetary and financial system, moving away from Western financial infrastructure.\\nGeopolitical Stance: BRICS is viewed by some as an alternative to Western-led institutions like those of the G7. The group seeks to build an alternative to what they perceive as the dominance of Western viewpoints in major multilateral organizations. However, there are internal divisions, particularly on issues like relations with the United States and geopolitical conflicts such as Russia\'s invasion of Ukraine.\\nChallenges: Despite its ambitions, BRICS has faced criticism for not uniting effectively as a global force, with some analysts suggesting that the group serves more for symbolic gestures than for substantial policy impact.\\nIn summary, BRICS is a coalition of emerging economies aiming to enhance their global economic and political influence, working towards reducing reliance on established Western financial systems and promoting multipolarity in international affairs.","sender":"AGENT","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]}],"destination":"destination_1","allowed_actions":[],"metadata":{"text":"Answer by Grok, expand to see full conversation"}}}},"destination_objects":{"destination_1":{"type":"browser","data":{"url_data":{"url":"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/i\\/grok\\/share\\/3LhHjLAQQN6lGlWzfAsgMo8B2","vanity":"Grok"}}}},"components":["details_1"]}', 'type': 'STRING'}}, {'key': 'card_url', 'value': {'scribe_key': 'card_url', 'string_value': 'https://t.co/KDujRZNFbM', 'type': 'STRING'}}], 'card_platform': {'platform': {'audience': {'name': 'production'}, 'device': {'name': 'Swift', 'version': '12'}}}, 'name': 'unified_card', 'url': 'https://t.co/KDujRZNFbM', 'user_refs_results': []}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1885143885329920417'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1738291901000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, '